$$
\displaystyle\frac{a_1\ J \ \dots \ a_k\ J}{a\ J}
$$

we typically need to show:

$$
\displaystyle\frac{\mathcal{P}(a_1)\ \dots\ \mathcal{P}(a_k)}{\mathcal{P}(a)}
$$

In this case, the ${fref("/01-programming-language-theory/02-concepts/instance-of-the-judgment-form.td")} $\mathcal{P}(a)$ is the **inductive conclusion**.
